---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

import { LEGAL } from "@/data/legal";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of Service for Edah Art. Governs use of the website, purchases of artworks, prints, and commissions. Includes pricing, shipping, returns, commissions, intellectual property, and governing law."
  noIndex={true}
  noFollow={true}
>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of <strong>{LEGAL.siteUrl}</strong> (the "Website")
    and any purchase of artworks, prints or commissions from <strong>{LEGAL.brand}</strong>, operated by <strong>{LEGAL.owner}</strong> ("we", "us", "our"), based in {LEGAL.address}. By using the Website or placing an order, you agree to
    these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Website.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Using the Website</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 18 years old, or have the consent of a parent or
    guardian, to place an order. You agree to use the Website lawfully and not
    to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>copy, scrape or harvest content from the Website in bulk;</li>
    <li>interfere with the Website's security or normal operation;</li>
    <li>
      submit false information or use another person's payment details without
      permission.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Artworks and product descriptions</h2>
  <p>
    My work is handmade. Colours may look different on your screen than in
    person, and small variations in texture, size and finish are part of the
    character of each piece. I take care to describe and photograph each item
    accurately, but I cannot guarantee that every detail will match your screen
    exactly. Original artworks are one-of-a-kind; prints may be produced in
    limited editions as described on the product page.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Prices and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices are shown in US dollars (USD) unless stated otherwise.</li>
    <li>
      Prices do not include shipping, taxes, or import duties unless stated.
      These are shown or calculated at checkout where possible.
    </li>
    <li>
      Payments are processed securely by {LEGAL.paymentProvider}. I do not
      receive or store your full card details.
    </li>
    <li>
      If I discover a pricing or listing error, I may correct it and contact
      you before proceeding; if you no longer wish to buy at the correct price,
      I will cancel the order and refund you in full.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Orders and availability</h2>
  <p>
    Placing an order is an offer to buy. I accept it when I send an order
    confirmation or dispatch the item. Because original works are one-of-a-kind,
    if a piece is no longer available when your order is processed I will tell
    you promptly and refund you in full.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Shipping and delivery</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      I ship using carriers such as {LEGAL.courier}. Delivery times are
      estimates, not guarantees, and may be affected by customs, weather or
      carrier delays.
    </li>
    <li>
      You are responsible for providing a correct and complete delivery address,
      and for any customs duties, import taxes or clearance fees charged by your
      country.
    </li>
    <li>
      Risk of loss or damage passes to you on delivery. If an item arrives
      damaged, please follow the steps in our <a href="/refund-policy">Refund &amp; Returns Policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Returns and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    My <a href="/refund-policy">Refund &amp; Returns Policy</a> forms part of these
    Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Commissions</h2>
  <p>
    Custom work is subject to the following, in addition to the rest of these
    Terms:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We will agree the subject, size, medium, price and estimated timeline with
      you in writing before work begins.
    </li>
    <li>
      A deposit of {LEGAL.commissionDepositPercent}% is required to begin a
      commission, with the balance due before the finished piece is shipped
      (unless we agree otherwise in writing).
    </li>
    <li>
      We will share a sketch or concept for your approval. Reasonable
      adjustments at that stage are included; major changes after approval may
      change the price and timeline.
    </li>
    <li>
      You keep creative trust in the artist: the final piece is an
      interpretation of the agreed brief, not an exact replica of any reference.
    </li>
    <li>
      Timelines are estimates and depend on how quickly you respond with
      feedback and approvals.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may photograph and share the finished work (for example in our
      portfolio and on social media) unless you ask us in writing not to.
    </li>
    <li>
      Cancellations and refunds for commissions are covered in the Refund &amp;
      Returns Policy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    All artworks, photographs, text, logos and other content on the Website are
    protected by copyright and belong to {LEGAL.owner} unless stated otherwise.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Buying a physical artwork</strong> gives you ownership of the object
      itself. It does not transfer copyright or the right to reproduce, publish, print
      or make merchandise from the artwork. You are free to display, gift or resell
      the physical piece.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Prints</strong> are sold for personal, non-commercial use.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may not copy, modify, distribute or use our images or artwork
      (including to train machine-learning models) without our written
      permission.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Your messages and submissions</h2>
  <p>
    If you send us messages, commission briefs or reference images, you confirm
    you have the right to share them and allow us to use them to respond to you
    and carry out the work. We will not publish your personal messages.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Third-party services and links</h2>
  <p>
    The Website may link to or display content from third parties (for example
    Instagram) and relies on providers such as payment processors and couriers.
    We are not responsible for their content, availability or policies, which
    are governed by their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, the Website is provided "as is" and
    we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for loss caused by
    events outside our reasonable control. Our total liability in connection
    with any order is limited to the amount you paid for that order.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits any liability, or any of your
    rights as a consumer, that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable
    law, including the Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Act 2018 of
    Nigeria.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    How we handle your personal information is explained in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the
    top shows when they last changed. Orders are governed by the Terms in force
    when you place them.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria. If
    you have a complaint, please contact us first so we can try to resolve it
    informally within 30 days. If that does not work, the courts of Lagos State
    have jurisdiction, without affecting any mandatory consumer rights you have
    under the laws of the country where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms? Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.email}`}>{LEGAL.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
